    "question": "I would recite a verse in prayer and then after that I would say what the verse means in English(to understand), is this permissible? (sometimes I say it in my heart.) For example, I would recite the first verse of Surah Fatiha, then after this I would say: &#8220;All praise is due to Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the Worlds.&#8221; Is this right, or permissible?",
    "title": "QUESTION: I would recite a verse in prayer and then after that I would say what the verse means in English(to understand), is this permissible? (sometimes I say it in my heart.) For example, I would recite the first verse of Surah Fatiha, then after this I would say: &#8220;All praise is due to Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the Worlds.&#8221; Is this right, or permissible?",
    "answer": "If you think about it in your heart, this is permissible but if you say it, it&#8217;s not permissible and the prayer would be invalid",
