    "id": 55728,
    "question": "We are reverts &#038; stay in kaafir area. I pray obligatory salah in congregation with my mother &#038; wife at home. Is it mandatory to give adhan &#038; iqama before congregational prayer at home? Are our prayers valid if we don&#8217;t give (1) iqama &#038; (2) adhan? Masjid is approximately 3.5kms away",
    "title": "QUESTION: We are reverts &#038; stay in kaafir area. I pray obligatory salah in congregation with my mother &#038; wife at home. Is it mandatory to give adhan &#038; iqama before congregational prayer at home? Are our prayers valid if we don&#8217;t give (1) iqama &#038; (2) adhan? Masjid is approximately 3.5kms away",
    "answer": "It&#8217;s not mandatory to give the adhan if its already given in any masjid in the city. Reciting the iqamah is a highly recommended sunnah but it&#8217;s not mandatory and the prayer is valid even if one skips it intentionally.",
