    "id": 50433,
    "question": "Some say if you don&#8217;t pray witr salah, the previous salah that you prayed that day will be invalid. Is it true? What about sunnah prayers, are they mandatory to pray?",
    "title": "QUESTION: Some say if you don&#8217;t pray witr salah, the previous salah that you prayed that day will be invalid. Is it true? What about sunnah prayers, are they mandatory to pray?",
    "answer": "What they have said is absolutely baseless and fabricated. It is not mandatory to pray as these are voluntary prayers. However, you would lose a great deal of reward if you don&#8217;t pray them but you&#8217;re not sinful and your prayers are valid. Prophet salla Allahu alaihi wa sallam never used to miss Witr and 2 rakahs of sunnah of fajr even while he was traveling, however these are not obligatory.",
