    "id": 49756,
    "question": "It says at the end of the fard prayer you should make dua  but I was taught to do the dua after you finish the fard and sunnah, then do dhikr then dua// is this correct too?",
    "title": "It says at the end of the fard prayer you should make dua  but I was taught to do the dua after you finish the fard and sunnah, then do dhikr then dua// is this correct too?",
    "answer": "No. The dua should be made after completing the prayer, just before making salam. It&#8217;s time to make the prescribed dhikr after you conclude the fard prayer (after salam). After finishing fard salah, it&#8217;s time for making the prescribed dhikr. The best time in salah to make dua is in your sujood and in the last tashahhud before making salam. It&#8217;s an innovation to make dua after salah.",
