    "id": 35974,
    "question": "Sheikh, after obligatory prayer is it allowed to make Dua (supplication) individually by raising hands or is it an innovation?",
    "title": "Sheikh, after obligatory prayer is it allowed to make Dua (supplication) individually by raising hands or is it an innovation?",
    "answer": "Yes, it&#8217;s an innovation to raise the hands and make dua after salah. If you make the dua after salah once in a blue moon without raising hands, it&#8217;s OK but you must not make it a habit as this is the time for doing the prescribed dhikr and you should make dua in your sujood and in the last tashahud before making Salam. https://youtu.be/hYToZVeAl20 &nbsp;",
    "answer_preview": "Yes, it&#8217;s an innovation to raise the hands and make dua after salah. If you make the dua after salah once in a blue moon without raising hands, it&#8217;s OK but you must not make it a habit as this is the time for doing the prescribed dhikr and you should make dua in your sujood and in the last tashahud before making Salam. https://youtu.be/hYToZVeAl20 &nbsp;",
