    "id": 32388,
    "question": "In the world Most of the normal peoples who missed fardh salah intentionally and non intentionally.so they have more pending salah.In our location(India) i asked this question what to do with the pending salah to my alim.he replied you should not do sunnath salah instead you want balance your pending fardh salah.what&#8217;s the correct ruling and answer for this ?",
    "title": "In the world Most of the normal peoples who missed fardh salah intentionally and non intentionally.so they have more pending salah.In our location(India) i asked this question what to do with the pending salah to my alim.he replied you should not do sunnath salah instead you want balance your pending fardh salah.what&#8217;s the correct ruling and answer for this ?",
    "answer": "It is not permissible to pray the prayers that you missed deliberately, without any reason. You must repent sincerely to Allah and never do such a major sin again and do a lot of voluntary good deeds and worship, especially night prayers to try and compensate for the missed prayers.",
