    "answer": "Seeking refuge in Allah (aauzubillah hi&#8230;) in the beginning is sufficient. You simply say bismillah before reciting fateha and other surahs in the following rak&#8217;ahs. If you get distracted by Satan in your salah, you simply seek refuge in Allah and drily spit towards your left.",
    "answer_preview": "Seeking refuge in Allah (aauzubillah hi&#8230;) in the beginning is sufficient. You simply say bismillah before reciting fateha and other surahs in the following rak&#8217;ahs. If you get distracted by Satan in your salah, you simply seek refuge in Allah and drily spit towards your left.",
    "slug": "is-it-mandatory-to-say-auzubillamishatan-rajeem-bismillah-raheem-in-the-beginning-of-every-rakah-or-is-it-that-i-should-only-say-bimillahi-rahem-and-carry-on-in-the-rakahs-i-believe-that-we-say",
    "date": "2018-12-21T08:07:07",
    "modified": "2018-12-21T08:07:07",
    "link": "https://www.assimalhakeem.net/is-it-mandatory-to-say-auzubillamishatan-rajeem-bismillah-raheem-in-the-beginning-of-every-rakah-or-is-it-that-i-should-only-say-bimillahi-rahem-and-carry-on-in-the-rakahs-i-believe-that-we-say/",
    "excerpt": "ANSWER: Seeking refuge in Allah (aauzubillah hi&#8230;) in the beginning is sufficient. You simply say bismillah before reciting fateha and other surahs in the following rak&#8217;ahs.  If you get distracted by Satan in your salah, you simply seek refuge in Allah and drily spit towards your left.",
