    "question": "In salat when a woman raises her hands saying Allahu akbar before going to ruku and her abaya arm sleeves drop down a bit in that moment revealing her wrists and and a couple inches of her forearm is her prayer valid? If she has this abaya on should she just not raise her hands?please advise.",
    "title": "In salat when a woman raises her hands saying Allahu akbar before going to ruku and her abaya arm sleeves drop down a bit in that moment revealing her wrists and and a couple inches of her forearm is her prayer valid? If she has this abaya on should she just not raise her hands?please advise.",
    "answer": "Deliberately exposing her arms like this nullifies her prayers. She must ensure that it doesn&#8217;t expose her arms. Not raising her hands won&#8217;t affect her prayer, however, she should either wear sleeves underneath her abaya or tighten it from the wrist area so that it won&#8217;t go up.",
