    "id": 24465,
    "question": "My mom has artheritis. So she cannot sit on the ground. But she can stand and she can sit and prostrate for sujood on a flat elevated surface. Is it correct to be seated on the chair for the whole salah without standing?. Is this method of sujood that she does correct?",
    "title": "My mom has artheritis. So she cannot sit on the ground. But she can stand and she can sit and prostrate for sujood on a flat elevated surface. Is it correct to be seated on the chair for the whole salah without standing?. Is this method of sujood that she does correct?",
    "answer": "You cannot offer your prayers sitting without a legitimate reason as standing up in the standing position in salah is a pillar, without which your Salah is invalid. She can can sit on a chair for doing sujood. She should pray standing and do the ruku normally and when she has to make sujood she should sit on the chair and bend a little while keeping her hands on her knees or thighs.",
