    "id": 57782,
    "question": "Till 7 years my husband gave the zakath as i don&#8217;t work and he himself opted to do so . Also once when he was unable to pay it i sold some jewelry and paid the zakath. Now last year i gave most of my jewelry back to my parents saying i don&#8217;t need it and i want to return it back . When he learned about this he said either give me the zakath amount of all those years or the gold .",
    "title": "QUESTION: Till 7 years my husband gave the zakath as i don&#8217;t work and he himself opted to do so . Also once when he was unable to pay it i sold some jewelry and paid the zakath. Now last year i gave most of my jewelry back to my parents saying i don&#8217;t need it and i want to return it back . When he learned about this he said either give me the zakath amount of all those years or the gold .",
    "answer": "He has no right in asking for such a thing as he paid it as a gift and not as a loan. The prophet salla Allahu alaihi wa sallam said: the one who goes back on his gift is like a dog that vomits and then eats back its own vomit!",
