    "question": "My jewelry are with my in laws and after my marriage they did not give me and have kept with them.Do i need to consider them(jewelleries kept with inlaws) while calcualting my contribution to zakat?",
    "title": "My jewelry are with my in laws and after my marriage they did not give me and have kept with them.Do i need to consider them(jewelleries kept with inlaws) while calcualting my contribution to zakat?",
    "answer": "If its not in your possession and they would not give it to you even after you ask them to, in this case there&#8217;s no zakat on it for you. However, you must ask your husband to talk to your in laws and give that jewelry back to you and after that keep it in a locker in the bank and never give it to them no matter what. &nbsp;",
